{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/131073-breeding-a-flawed-concept-for-shapeshifters","id":131073,"title":"Breeding: A flawed concept for Shapeshifters?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-10T17:41:09-07:00","id":131073,"title":"Breeding: A flawed concept for Shapeshifters?","content":"So I've been reading through my Werewolf: the Forsaken rule book and found out that for one shapeshifter to breed with another, even a member of their own species, is apparently forbidden. In Forsaken, this results in a Spirit Wolf, who is among the most deadly enemies of the Forsaken. For the old WoD, it resulted in a Metis who are apparently outcasts and considered to be inferior life forms.<br /> <br /> <br /> I ask the question: WHY!?<br /> <br /> According to both versions of the game, when an ordinary human looks upon the bestial forms of a shapeshifter, they go insane and suffer from amnesia. In the old version they could apparently mate with wild animals, but in the new book I think they can only mate with sentient beings. So this pretty much means they are forced to breed with humans, a race who is terrified of them and incapable of understanding their true nature or purpose.<br /> <br /> This is why I think the concept of mating between two shapeshifters needs to be reworked.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 1 - The shapeshifter is often called away from their family to deal with matters of the spirit world and has to keep their true nature a secret from humans. The spirits don't give a damn about modern life for humans, and they aren't just going to wait until the shapeshifter has some free time on their paws before they decide to start causing trouble.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2 - The shapeshifter has no idea which of their children have inherited the gene until it awakens, and therefore the child has practically no warning ahead of time. They might change in public or in a similarly inopportune moment and be scared out of their damn minds about what is happening.<br /> <br /> 3 - Not only must the parent train their child in the ways of their kind, but they now have two shapeshifters in the family who have to keep their true nature a secret.<br /> <br /> <br /> 4 - Unless they are extremely lucky, I see this recipe ending in a disaster every time. The family is destroyed either because of secrecy and lack of trust, or something from the spirit world takes out the humans when the shapeshifters can't protect them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The pros of allowing shapeshifters to mate with each other are as follows<br /> <br /> <br /> 1 - No need to keep secrets within the family. This also staves off the possibility of your family discovering your secret accidentally out of burning curiosity.<br /> <br /> 2 - The child can be warned from an early age what to expect during the first change and thus have much better preparations before it occurs than simply having an emotional breakdown.<br /> <br /> 3 - The whole family is comprised of shapeshifters, so the whole family is ready to throw down if a spirit comes knocking at their door.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Somebody tell me if there is a reason this rule is put into place, because I don't understand it. Most, if not all supernatural beings want to keep humans in the dark, so mating with them seems like the worst possible way to do that!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now I could understand this being the case if being a shapeshifter was some kind of supernatural curse like it is in mythology. Nature's way of punishing the shapeshifters for daring to strengthen the bloodline instead of diluting it. But the truth is, being a member of the changing breeds is NOT a curse, NOR a disease, it is a spiritual heritage. A higher calling than the mundane and corrupting life of a human. It is a GIFT, so why should keeping that gift alive be punished instead of rewarded?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T17:47:26-07:00","id":131083,"title":"","content":"From what I could gather from the text, it was to heighten dramatic tension and conflict among the <i>Uratha</i> as a sort of &quot;human vs. animal&quot; paradox \u2014 the needs and minds of humans, but the instincts and rage of killer beasts. That being said, if you pick up <i>Forsaken Chronicler's Guide</i>, there's some rules changes in there that allows you to avoid the problems you're thinking of. I also believe the concept of a Ghost Wolf was scrapped for the Idigam Chronicles, to the point now where humans may run in packs with werewolves if the werewolves choose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T18:02:12-07:00","id":131097,"title":"","content":"It still doesn't make any sense to me, though. Especially the old world version. Where it heavily references how humans are the source of evil and corruption in the world. . And that humanity vs animal complex makes even less sense. Both in the animal kingdom and in human civilization, a species naturally chooses to mate with its own kind. Sure we occasionally get funny videos on the internet of dogs trying to hump cats, or whatever, but these are usually rare and accidental incidents, not a natural instinct.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In my mind, I envision that as Gaia saying<br /> <br /> &quot;My children, you have been chosen to be my protectors. You must ensure the world works the way it was meant to do so. You must stop the humans who pollute my waters and defile my earth. Yours is a noble calling, a chance to rise above the corruptive influence of the Wyrm and restore paradise to the land. Oh but I want you to go out and start having children with these vile humans. Anyone of you who takes a fellow shifter as a mate is to be shunned and outcast, the child stoned to death at birth!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Ummm, kind of getting mixed signals here, Gaia!<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't own the Idigam Chronicles, so I don't know about any of the rule changes you mentioned. But for me personally, I would like to throw out this concept entirely in my stories. Yeah, it leaves a gaping hole in one of the traditions / laws / oaths or whatever, but I personally think it makes more sense from a logical perspective. If it is not a curse, if it is a gift or some manner of higher calling, there should be no reason why spreading it should be punishable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-10-2014, 09:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T18:10:16-07:00","id":131102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/131073-breeding-a-flawed-concept-for-shapeshifters?p=131097#post131097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't own the Idigam Chronicles, so I don't know about any of the rule changes you mentioned. But for me personally, I would like to throw out this concept entirely in my stories. Yeah, it leaves a gaping hole in one of the traditions / laws / oaths or whatever, but I personally think it makes more sense from a logical perspective. If it is not a curse, if it is a gift or some manner of higher calling, there should be no reason why spreading it should be punishable.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one owns Idigam Chronicles yet, it hasn't been published, but according to the writer, werewolves can have children with other werewolves. If you want to expand on the matter, feel free to apply for some freelance work with them:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\"> Page not found &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> For what it's worth, while I don't care about Werewolf the Apocalypse's reasons, I believe it works in Werewolf the Forsaken just fine, except for the Harmony thing. You should probably read more about the subject if you're going to post about it demanding reworking. Humans are not incapable of understanding the purpose of werewolves, they're just unlikely to appreciate it until shown. Primal Urge does scare people, but it's the equivalent of a person seeming like a dangerous individual, and with a merit can be turned into a good thing. Lunacy appears when they shapeshift.<br /> <br /> And while it may have only happened once, it is conceivable for a werewolf to mate with a wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-10-2014, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T18:22:15-07:00","id":131148,"title":"","content":"Ah, so it is possible for them to mate with each other? Good then. I was just asking this because, I thought the idea of them being forced to breed with humans was ridiculous and posed way too many problems down the line.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I kept calling them shapeshifters, because I know there were other species in the old WoD, but I don't know if that continues to hold true in Forsaken, or if they're just wolves. Ratkin appear to have been changed into some kind of animal spirit instead of being a separate breed of shifter. Or maybe I was just reading that wrong, but either way, the story of Father Wolf and Mother Luna failed to mention the possibilities of other shifters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T18:27:51-07:00","id":131151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/131073-breeding-a-flawed-concept-for-shapeshifters?p=131148#post131148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, so it is possible for them to mate with each other? Good then. I was just asking this because, I thought the idea of them being forced to breed with humans was ridiculous and posed way too many problems down the line.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I kept calling them shapeshifters, because I know there were other species in the old WoD, but I don't know if that continues to hold true in Forsaken, or if they're just wolves. Ratkin appear to have been changed into some kind of animal spirit instead of being a separate breed of shifter. Or maybe I was just reading that wrong, but either way, the story of Father Wolf and Mother Luna failed to mention the possibilities of other shifters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I highly, highly suggest you look at the following books for more information:<br /> <br /> - War Against the Pure (alternate shapeshifter ideas along with werewolf warfare)<br /> <br /> - Changing Breeds (one of nWoD's worst books, but full of redeemable ideas that can be fixed using War mechanics)<br /> <br /> - Blood of the Wolf (werewolf physiology)<br /> <br /> - Predators (what werewolves actually hunt)<br /> <br /> - Night Horrors (builds on Predators)<br /> <br /> Read those, and they should give you a bit more insight on what is what in W:tF. Just because it's not mentioned in the corebook doesn't mean it doesn't show up in the supplemental material. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T18:36:28-07:00","id":131152,"title":"","content":"Changing Breeds is for nWoD? I thought it was for the old version. I've been curious to read it, but thought I might have been wasting the time if it was no longer relevant. (I prefer the New World of Darkness, despite everyone I meet claiming Old WoD is superior.) I've also heard that Changing Breeds may have the ground work set for being able to create your own breed aside from what's already listed.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd be curious to try playing a different type of shapeshifter. The Rokea sound pretty awesome.<br /> <br /> <br /> Humans tried to nuke the whales.<br /> <br /> <br /> They nuked the sharks<br /> <br /> <br /> The sharks did not respond well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------<br /> <br /> Wait, now I'm confused. A bunch of wikis claim its for old WoD, and deals with Gaia and the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-10-2014, 09:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T18:47:48-07:00","id":131163,"title":"","content":"There are several different books called Changing Breeds. 'Players Guide to the Changing Breeds' is the old Classic WoD book - this was revised, updated and expanded in W20 Changing Breeds. World of Darkness: Changing Breeds is the New WoD book for different shapeshifters. As others have mentioned, it's not very good, but can be mined for ideas.<br /> <br /> Edit: From your posts, Nyrufa, you really have your WoDs mixed up. Rokea are very much cWoD. Most (all?) of the themes from Werewolf the Apocalypse are not relevant to Werewolf the Forsaken. (Or the nWoD for that matter.) Buying various books will give you the most complete information, but a quick Google/Wikipedia search will help you sort out the two WoDs and what belongs where.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 05-10-2014, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T18:48:03-07:00","id":131164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/131073-breeding-a-flawed-concept-for-shapeshifters?p=131152#post131152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, now I'm confused. A bunch of wikis claim its for old WoD, and deals with Gaia and the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, a number of nWoD titles share names with oWoD titles. You do not want to use the mechanics in nWoD Changing Breeds for your shifters, as they are fundamentally broken; use the ones in War Against the Pure's fourth chapter instead.<br /> <br /> This is the book I mentioned: <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/51348/World-of-Darkness-Changing-Breeds\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/produc...hanging-Breeds</a><br /> <br /> This is War Against the Pure: <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/25702/The-War-Against-the-Pure\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/produc...ainst-the-Pure</a><br /> <br /> This is the Werewolf Translation Guide to bring stuff from oWoD into nWoD: <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/100710/Werewolf-Translation-Guide\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/produc...nslation-Guide</a><br /> <br /> And these were the suggestions from a dev for bringing stuff like Rokea into nWoD, which had to be cut from the Translation Guide for space: <a href=\"http://www.zeropointinformation.com/blog/2012/fera-translation-guide/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.zeropointinformation.com/...slation-guide/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T19:04:20-07:00","id":131175,"title":"","content":"Thanks, now I know which one to look for. I watched a video of some guy reviewing the Makole source book and he considered it to be garbage because the book is written in a manner that seams like it's being told from the perspective of a Makole. He said you have to flip through the book and translate practically every sentence with the index.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T19:15:10-07:00","id":131197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/131073-breeding-a-flawed-concept-for-shapeshifters?p=131175#post131175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, now I know which one to look for. I watched a video of some guy reviewing the Makole source book and he considered it to be garbage because the book is written in a manner that seams like it's being told from the perspective of a Makole. He said you have to flip through the book and translate practically every sentence with the index.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a recommended reading list around here somewhere of books that are good for the newbie Forsaken player. I'm not sure where it is, but if you make a new post in the Forsaken forum and ask, people will be glad to help point you in the right direction to get started with. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T19:38:18-07:00","id":131298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/131073-breeding-a-flawed-concept-for-shapeshifters#post131073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Somebody tell me if there is a reason this rule is put into place, because I don't understand it. Most, if not all supernatural beings want to keep humans in the dark, so mating with them seems like the worst possible way to do that!</div> </div> </div> </div>My group scrapped the human mates pretty early. But I can see what they were going for. All of the supernaturals have a reason to hang around with humans. If not for the mating werewolves would have none. Without them its can be pretty easy for all the tribes to devolve into different shades of the red talons. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1303-zap-rowsdower","name":"zap rowsdower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1303_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T19:44:49-07:00","id":131328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/131073-breeding-a-flawed-concept-for-shapeshifters?p=131197#post131197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is a recommended reading list around here somewhere of books that are good for the newbie Forsaken player. I'm not sure where it is, but if you make a new post in the Forsaken forum and ask, people will be glad to help point you in the right direction to get started with. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I own the core rule book, vamp book, and wolf book for nWoD, but don't have any others. And I only have those because I bought them at the Mall of Georgia, the only store I ever saw that still carried them in print, rather than buying them online. Wish I had picked up mage while I had the chance, and Changeling too.<br /> <br /> <br /> I do have a question as to how complicated each system is. I first got into WoD because of the Bloodlines PC game. I'm most familiar with the Vampire setting, since it transitioned pretty easily between oWoD and nWoD for me, but I don't know anything else about the old world. The Werewolf Forsaken book is extremely complicated for me. Having to deal with bans, and spirits, and the spirit world, and auspices and gifts, and tribes. Maybe its just because I didn't have a crash course game to teach me the basics (nice job whoever canceled Heart of Gaia...), but I'm already introduced to the idea of ghouls, clans, covenants, and so on. So I find vampires easier to handle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T06:44:27-07:00","id":132126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/131073-breeding-a-flawed-concept-for-shapeshifters?p=131328#post131328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do have a question as to how complicated each system is. I first got into WoD because of the Bloodlines PC game. I'm most familiar with the Vampire setting, since it transitioned pretty easily between oWoD and nWoD for me, but I don't know anything else about the old world. The Werewolf Forsaken book is extremely complicated for me. Having to deal with bans, and spirits, and the spirit world, and auspices and gifts, and tribes. Maybe its just because I didn't have a crash course game to teach me the basics (nice job whoever canceled Heart of Gaia...), but I'm already introduced to the idea of ghouls, clans, covenants, and so on. So I find vampires easier to handle.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what it sounds like, you've dived into the games a little too early without reading and understanding the material. Forsaken is complicated a little bit, yes, but Apocalypse was to some degree as well. The book attempted to nerf down Werewolves to something manageable in the nWoD, all while giving them a flavour more distinct than Apocalypse. It's one of the weaker lines of nWoD, but Idigam Chronicles looks like it may change a number of aspects the fandom has griped about. It's our equivalent of Werewolf: the Apocalypse 1.0. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The easiest games to get into are Mortal, its supplements and then Hunter, which is basically Mortals+. Hunter introduces the concept of more factions and powers without going too heavy on the power stats, and is easy to practice with to create characters that are more than just human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T10:09:31-07:00","id":132361,"title":"","content":"Personally, I think either way of using the werewolves was fine to me. The old world had somewhat more appeal, they're chosen by nature itself to take up a higher calling and keep the world from imploding upon itself. In the new world, they're the descendants of Kin Killers who want to keep the world in check while atoning for the crimes of their ancestors.<br /> <br /> <br /> I also want to point out hat I think the overall lore behind the nWoD appears much more fleshed out than its oWoD counterpart. Now again, I have only rudimentary understanding of the old world, so forgive me if I'm wrong. But it sounds to me like each game was designed to be played separately from each other. When I started reading up the origin story of each of these races, I got very confused because they all seemed to have contradicting legends about the creation of the world and life in general. Vampires claim the story of Cain and take their origins from the bible, which would indicate the world only being about 6,000 years old.<br /> <br /> Then you have the Changing Breeds who claim to be children of Gaia, and the Makole ruled the land in the time of dinosaurs, which would mean the world is millions of years old.<br /> <br /> <br /> Then you have the Mages and Changelings.... okay, I know absolutely nothing about how the old world version of them worked, but I'm guessing they had similar tales.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the new version, they seem to have removed a great deal of these conflicting stories. For example, the vampires no longer have a Cain based story and indeed, nobody knows where the clans originated from. As far as they're aware, they could be as old as humanity itself. The Werewolves talk about the super continent of Pangaea which suggests they may be the first of the supernatural races.<br /> <br /> <br /> The mages are descended from Atlantis, so they came about at some point during human history, instead of the beginning of creation.<br /> <br /> Changelings are humans who were abducted, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T10:19:04-07:00","id":132368,"title":"","content":"You are right: nWoD was made with crossovers in mind. It's written that a unified cosmology is workable and completely optional if you so choose; a good word to described nWoD is &quot;toolbox&quot; or &quot;toolkit&quot;. oWoD...at the end, oWoD was more tangled in its continuity than Changeling's Hedge was on a bad day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T19:44:44-07:00","id":133097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/131073-breeding-a-flawed-concept-for-shapeshifters?p=132368#post132368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are right: nWoD was made with crossovers in mind. It's written that a unified cosmology is workable and completely optional if you so choose; a good word to described nWoD is &quot;toolbox&quot; or &quot;toolkit&quot;. oWoD...at the end, oWoD was more tangled in its continuity than Changeling's Hedge was on a bad day.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Okay well I have tried looking around and there is pretty much zero information on the content of these books, without them simply being directions to buy the books myself. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> What are the new breeds that are introduced to the game? I know the books give you information on how you can build your own, but I understand they introduced 5 pre-generated ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T06:28:30-07:00","id":133642,"title":"","content":"Nyrufa, it looks like you're having some confusion. There's a lot of WoD material (new and old), so that's understandable! Let me try to help sort it out.<br /> <br /> It looks like your initial questions (about werewolf breeding) have been answered. So I'll just address the WoD differences here.<br /> <br /> So, basically, we're looking at at least two sets of books here. The first set is the &quot;classic&quot; World of Darkness (or cWoD), which consists of Vampire: the Masquerade, Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Mage: the Ascension, Changeling: the Dreaming, Wraith: the Oblivion, Mummy: the Resurrection, Hunter: the Reckoning, and Demon: the Fallen. There are a ton of books in that set, through the various game lines. Books like Rokea, Mokole, and so forth? They go with Werewolf: the Apocalypse. They have no reference to Werewolf: the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> In 2004, the cWoD ended (although more on that in a bit), and the World of Darkness (usually called the &quot;new&quot; World of Darkness, or nWoD) began. The system was changed a bit, and there was (and continues to be) a greater focus on the different species being able to play well together mechanically. Even so, each book is focused on its own subject matter first and foremost. To date, the game lines are: core mortals (some call this the &quot;blue line&quot;), Vampire: the Requiem, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Mage: the Awakening, Promethean: the Created, Changeling: the Lost, Hunter: the Vigil, Geist: the Sin-Eaters, Mummy: the Curse, and Demon: the Descent. There is a Changing Breeds book, for the &quot;blue line,&quot; meaning that it is usable or not with other games at the Storyteller's decision.<br /> <br /> Those are the core pieces. In 2011, out came Vampire: the Masquerade 20th Anniversary Edition. Werewolf: the Apocalypse 20th Anniversary Edition followed it, and Mage: the Ascension 20th Anniversary Edition is next. These anniversary edition books updated both rules and setting for those cWoD games. Further new supplements are based from these books.<br /> <br /> On the nWoD side, we so far have God-Machine Chronicle and Blood &amp; Smoke: the Strix Chronicle, for the core line and Vampire: the Requiem respectively. We're in the process of writing The Idigam Chronicle for Werewolf, and The Fallen World Chronicle seems to be in development (I'm not on that team, so I don't know where they're at in terms of the process). These books update both the rules and setting for the nWoD. In addition to those books, Demon: the Descent is written using the GMC rules set.<br /> <br /> Now, to chat specifically about the Changing Breeds books, as you're interested, there are a grand total of three.<br /> <br /> First, we have the Player's Guide to the Changing Breeds. This book is for the original Werewolf: the Apocalypse. To get a look at the cover: <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/3364/Players-Guide-to-the-Changing-Breeds?it=1\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/produc...ng-Breeds?it=1</a><br /> <br /> Then, we have W20 Changing Breeds: <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/121087/W20-Changing-Breeds\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/produc...hanging-Breeds</a><br /> <br /> And finally, there is Changing Breeds for the nWoD: <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/51348/World-of-Darkness-Changing-Breeds\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/produc...hanging-Breeds</a><br /> <br /> That's just to give you an idea of what all the covers look like (in case you hadn't seen them previously). So if you're playing Apocalypse, you want the first one. If you're using the W20 book, you want the second one. And if you want to put other breeds into your Werewolf: the Forsaken game, I would very much suggest that you use War Against the Pure instead of Changing Breeds. There are...issues with the latter book, I've found. <br /> <br /> Hope this is at least a helpful start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T10:37:31-07:00","id":134042,"title":"","content":"Thank you to everyone who has answered my questions, and put up with my newbie lack of information. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]